# Line endings, pinned so every clone agrees (from methodica-math-percent-08 / ratio-01).
#
# Every text blob in the index is already LF except the two translation CSVs (below), so
# this renormalises nothing in history. `eol=lf` additionally pins the WORKING TREE to LF
# on Windows, where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check out CRLF. Packages are
# assembled from the working tree, so this is what makes them byte-identical to their
# commit whoever builds them (Documentation/reporting-and-resume §11.1).

* text=auto eol=lf

# The translation CSVs are exports stored with CRLF (translation/*.csv) — kept byte-for-byte
# as delivered; never normalised.
*.csv   -text

# Explicit binary, so auto-detection is never the only thing guarding media.
*.ttf   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.mp4   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.pdf   binary

# SVG is XML — text, never binary.
*.svg   text eol=lf
